# Same collision as 03, but the two users are introduced in the opposite
# order, which swaps their fixed clientIDs (see scenario.mjs). If the forced
# outcome flips, "who wins" is decided by clientID -- NOT by which edit came
# later or which side was merged into which. Characterization, not a spec:
# in the real app clientIDs are random per browser session.

doc master
  heading level=1 "Title"

branch review from master

as bob   on review  set p1 level=3
as alice on master  set p1 level=2

merge review -> master
expect merged false
expect conflict attribute level

merge review -> master force
show master
